    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (3/3, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nTelephone is now stored and returned in **E.164 form** rather than as a 10\u2011digit string, with duplicate detection comparing those E.164 values.\n\n**New \u2014 `OwnerTelephone` helper** (`rest/function/owner/OwnerTelephone.java`): the single normalizer. It strips spaces, dashes and brackets; keeps a leading `+` and country code when present; otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0` from the national digits; then requires `+` followed by 8\u201315 digits, throwing `InvalidTelephoneException` (\u2192 400) when it can't. So `0412 345 678` \u2192 `+61412345678` and `+64 21 123 456` \u2192 `+6421123456`.\n\n**`ValidateOwnerFields`** (POST): replaced the \"strip to exactly 10 digits\" rule with `OwnerTelephone.toE164(...)`, storing the E.164 value.\n\n**`EnsureTelephoneUnique`** (POST duplicate check): now canonicalizes both the request and each existing owner to E.164 before comparing, instead of comparing bare digits.\n\n**`ValidateOwner`** (PUT): now also normalizes the telephone to E.164, so updates store the same form the entity constraint requires.\n\n**`Owner` entity**: telephone constraint changed from `@Digits`/`^[0-9]{10}$` to `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$` (removed the now-unused `@Digits` import) \u2014 needed because `spring-boot-starter-validation` validates the entity on persist.\n\n**`openapi.yml`**: relaxed the generated DTO's telephone `pattern` from `^[0-9]*$` to `^[+0-9 ()-]+$` so raw input (with `+`, spaces, dashes, brackets) survives the `@Valid` gate on the PUT path and reaches the normalizer; updated the description/example to E.164.\n\n**`InvalidTelephoneException`**: updated the message/Javadoc to describe the E.164 rule.\n\nSeed data (`+61`-less legacy numbers) and the DB column (`VARCHAR(20)`) are unaffected \u2014 legacy values are canonicalized on the fly during the duplicate check, and E.164 strings fit the column width.\n\nOne scope note: I extended E.164 normalization to the PUT path as well, since the entity-level constraint change would otherwise reject legacy-format updates. The three new acceptance tests exercise only POST + GET, which all pass, along with the rest of the suite.",
